This lab extends my previous work from Lab 3 by transforming textual reviews into structured, numerical features that can be used for machine learning.

1. Loading the Data

The curated dataset was loaded from the Gold layer using Spark’s Delta format:

abfss://lakehouse@goodreadreviews60312547.dfs.core.windows.net/gold/curated_reviews

2. Cleaning and Normalization

A cleaned_review column was created by: Converting text to lowercase.

Removing punctuation, emojis, URLs, and extra spaces.

Filtering out short or empty reviews.

3. Feature Extraction

The following features were generated:

Feature	Description
review_length_chars	Number of characters in the review text
review_length_words	Number of words in the review text
sentiment_score	Sentiment polarity (−1 negative → +1 positive) using VADER

4. Saving the Final Dataset

The enriched dataset was saved in the Gold layer under:

abfss://lakehouse@goodreadreviews60312547.dfs.core.windows.net/gold/features_v2/

5. Verification

The table was reloaded, and schema inspection confirmed the presence of all engineered features with valid data types.

6. Outcome

The resulting dataset is clean, feature-rich, and ready for the next stage of analysis (model training in Lab 5).
The features are clearly named, consistently typed, and reflect meaningful text-derived metrics.
